#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_dash_modern_mobile.py — fence DASH_MODERN_MOBILE_20261007
# (requires the dashboard chain on main: DASH_MODERN → … → FLEET_CHART_V2 → FLEET_MARKS)
#
# The Modern dashboard on phones (Tailscale / mobile browser). Until now
# Dashboard.jsx sent every phone to the Legacy page regardless of the setting.
# Now Settings → App Settings → Dashboard layout applies on phones too, and
# Modern has a compact layout below 768 px:
#   header      date, session pill, feed dot; NIFTY/BANKNIFTY badges swipe
#   KPIs        one card per book that traded today (idle book not shown):
#               hero MTM, realised · unrealised, then Net · From peak ·
#               Charges · Week P/L · Month P/L, and "N of 14 traded today"
#   chart       same Fleet | Grid views and collapse; legend chips in one
#               swipeable row; 2-column grid; touch scrubbing (pointer events,
#               touch-action pan-y — sideways drag reads, vertical swipe
#               scrolls), tooltip pinned to the top of the plot, clears 2.5 s
#               after lift; four time ticks
#   blotter     a list of cards (name + book, MTM, state, path, R / U /
#               trades / charges / stop, last event) + idle chips; tapping a
#               card, chip or grid cell focuses the strategy and scrolls its
#               panel into view
#   panel       StrategyHost respects rail=false on phones too (no chip rail
#               under Modern); a panel wider than the phone (TSG legs table)
#               scrolls sideways inside its own box instead of widening the page
# Desktop is unchanged (verified). Legacy on a phone is unchanged.
#
#   frontend  components/fleet/FleetChart.jsx       whole-file, guarded by the pre-image hash
#             components/fleet/FleetKpis.jsx        anchored (MobileKpis + branch)
#             components/fleet/FleetBlotter.jsx     anchored (FleetCards + branch)
#             pages/ModernDashboard.jsx             anchored
#             components/StrategyHost.jsx           anchored (mobile rail honours `rail`)
#             pages/Dashboard.jsx                   anchored (phones follow the setting)
#
# Deploy: ./desktop/build-scalp.sh frontend, relaunch, then reload the page on
# the phone (the shell is served no-cache). Relaunching restarts the backend
# too, so do it before 09:00 or after 15:40 IST on a trading day.
#
# Run ONLY this script:
#   cd /Users/anbu/dev/scalp-app && python3 apply_dash_modern_mobile.py [--allow-dirty]
